      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you—when agency slips away, even the choice to end the waiting feels like it’s been taken from you. But that’s the lie of the waiting room: it makes you forget that you’re still the one who can walk out, even if the door is heavy. You don’t have to find a reason to stay; you just have to find the one thing that makes the clock stop feeling like a judge. And if that thing is a single, quiet breath, that’s still a choice.",
